                <pb facs="0371" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg273"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51 Salt Funds/70: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-02T17:00:00+08:00">October 2, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 4—9:05 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>872. Legation’s 486, June 23, 6 p.m. Following from American Consul General at
                    Tientsin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“According to the statement of Foreign District Inspector of the Changlu
                            district on September 22nd he effected the remittance to Shanghai for
                            the service of foreign loan obligations secured on the salt revenue the
                            sum of $649,290.20 local currency representing the <pb facs="0372"
                                n="274" xml:id="pg274"/> amount of the Changlu loan quotas
                            accumulated at Tientsin since May last.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
